{"id": "biz-5", "headline": "AI speeds early drug development at big pharma", "source": "STAT News", "url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/20/sanofi-eyeing-insmed-ai-speeding-drug-development/", "published": "2026-11-20", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Artificial intelligence has sped early-stage drug development at some of the world's largest drugmakers this year, cutting by as much as half the time it takes to produce new molecules and move them into the clinic, according to a Reuters report summarized by STAT. Top scientists at Bristol Myers Squibb, Novartis, Eli Lilly, Sanofi, Novo Nordisk and AstraZeneca say they have moved beyond less glamorous AI tasks such as preparing regulatory filings. They now use it to design molecules, sort out the most promising candidates and identify safety risks. If the gains hold, new medicines could reach trials sooner. Source: STAT News."], "qr": {"n": 37, "rows": ["1111111011110111101010100010101111111", "1000001000011110100100000000101000001", "1011101001010100000011000111101011101", "1011101000110011110011011110001011101", "1011101000111110011100001000001011101", "1000001001010110110001010100001000001", "1111111010101010101010101010101111111", "0000000011001010101000010110000000000", "1101101001001111010000001001001000001", "0000010100100011000100010001110110010", "0011101010001011001000011011101111111", "0100110111000011011000000001000100100", "1000011111100110100010001010101101011", "1000110010101001100001010011010011110", "1100011000100011000101000011101110011", "0100110001101110000000001001010100101", "0111001000011001000010101101111001111", "0000010101010001011110100011110101000", "0010111011101111000101010011100110001", "1010110110010100100100100101000011001", "0000111100110100111100001011011010011", "1011100011101101011100110011100111110", "1101101111010101010001110011011110101", "0011000111111100110010111010100001111", "1100111100111101000110100001001100001", "1010110001100111101001010011000011010", "110100100001